Standard procedure - except you rarely get to meet a demon lord in the
Sanctum. 

Every one of the purple "&"s (and Juiblex, too, IIRC) is a "covetous"
monster - can be seen by how they always flip to the stairs to heal,
then back to attack you. However, if one of the four unique items is
around on the level, their priority will be to grab it. If the item is
in the possession of another creature, they'll attack it in order to
acquire the object. If the covetous monster in question is peaceful
(Geryon, Dispater, Baalzebub, Asmodeus), it will still try to get a
bribe out of you, but since 3.4.0 a monster carrying one of the unique
items will always ask for a bribe so high that there's no chance of
paying them off - successfully paying them off can automatically lose
the game otherwise.

